  talking moved the ground under the four of them to 0.0763; doing something moved it to 0.1600.
  that is 2.1 times as much for the arm that did something, off a third as many turns.

  where the difference is, and where it is not:
    talking with nothing earned is worth exactly nothing. A neighbour talked at 3 times and not won round has familiarity but no trust, and familiarity multiplies, so its sentiment is 0.0000 -- which the tables above show for every attempt that missed.
    what one thing earns is trust, and that is where a deed and a persuasion can be put beside each other: the best trust either arm reached is in the table above, on a single edge, out of the same judged share bounded the same way.
    at their ceilings -- every one of the 3 rolls landing, which happens on 8.0% of roll seeds, and every answer the largest the engine allows -- 3 lines each reaches 0.2891, one line each reaches 0.1250, and 3 gifts reach 0.1850.
    so at the same number of happenings a gift beats the best persuasion there is, and what buys the 3-line arm its lead is familiarity rather than goodwill: 9 conversations put it at 0.578 against a single dealing's 0.250, off three times the turns.

